1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:05,800
This Christmas has me deeply reflecting on the authentic and true life of Jesus.

2
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:10,780
I'm Muslim, so I don't celebrate Christmas religiously.

3
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:18,840
But as the world tries to divide us, I want to highlight the things that make us have more in common, actually.

4
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:21,020
Because unity is power.

5
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:25,740
And Muslims love Jesus.

6
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:26,980
I don't know if you know this.

7
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,740
We love Jesus.

8
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:31,360
We call Jesus Sayyid Na'isa.

9
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:39,320
And the biggest difference between Islam and Christianity is that we don't believe Jesus is the Son of God, but we do believe he is the most important prophet.

10
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:43,700
He's actually mentioned more times in the Quran than Prophet Muhammad.

11
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:45,820
And we call him Sayyid Na'isa.

12
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:49,640
So anytime you meet someone named Isa, you'll be like, wow, you're named Jesus.

13
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:59,160
And yeah, I mean, this year, like, my heart is totally broken, along with a lot of us, like, mourning and fighting for the freedom of Palestine.

14
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:09,260
But also reflecting on the story of Sayyid Na'isa, Jesus, and, you know, being born, fleeing persecution, fleeing genocide.

15
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:14,980
At the same time seeing Palestinian children being pulled out of the rubble.

16
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:26,960
And even though I don't celebrate Christmas religiously, I really welcome this opportunity to reflect on Jesus and the messages and lessons that he brought.

17
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:28,240
Free Palestine.

18
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:28,440
Free Palestine.

